      <h2>How to Compare Resorts</h2>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Look beyond the photos</h3>
        <p>A resort may look appealing online but still be a poor fit for your group. Compare the total trip cost, room occupancy rules, location, transportation options, meal arrangements, cancellation terms, and any age restrictions.</p>
        <p>Check whether the advertised amenities are included in the room price. A low base rate can become expensive if meals, airport transfers, and activities are extra.</p>
        <h3>Agree on the budget first</h3>
        <p>Ask each traveler to set a comfortable spending limit before selecting accommodations. A shared budget helps avoid disagreements and keeps the trip accessible to more friends.</p>
      </div>
